# "During any turn you attacked with a Rogue" asks what the attacker was as it was declared (CR 508.1). Robber of the Rich
# attacks on turn 1 and exiles Lightning Bolt. On turn 3 Bot1 attacks with Ornithopter alone, then casts Arcane Adaptation
# naming Rogue: the Ornithopter is a Rogue now, but was not as it attacked, so the Bolt cannot be cast (the refusal). On
# turn 5 the Ornithopter, a Rogue by then, attacks again, and Bot1 casts the Bolt with Mox Ruby (the control).
[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Island
Robber of the Rich
Ornithopter
Arcane Adaptation
Island x20
[Bot2 Deck]
Island x7
Lightning Bolt
Island x20
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Robber of the Rich.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Robber of the Rich > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Exile.Count = 1
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Arcane Adaptation.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Rogue)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Subtypes = Rogue; Thopter
! Bot1.Exile.Lightning Bolt.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Exile.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
[Expect]
Turn = 5
Stack.Count = 0
Exile.Count = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Island; Island
Bot2.Life = 15
